jury selection begins this morning in  the federal trial of three fired  minneapolis police officers facing civil  rights charges in the george floyd case  thomas lane j alexander king  and two tao were all at the scene when  derek chovin killed floyd by kneeling on  his neck for more than nine minutes nine  minutes and 29 seconds chauvin was  convicted of murder in a separate state  trial last spring now he has pleaded  guilty to one of the federal charges  mola lange's at the federal courthouse  in saint paul where the other three men  will now go on trial  we're back in session and on the record  unlike the trial last spring where court  cameras captured derek chauvin as  prosecutors successfully made their case  this trial won't be broadcast former  minneapolis police officers thomas lane  jay alexander king and two tao are  charged with willfully depriving george  floyd of his civil rights attorney and  legal analyst joe tamborino what is the  defense's argument here the defense's  argument is twofold number one that they  did not willfully try to violate the  rights of mr floyd and secondly that  they had no part in what mr chauvin was  doing video of the deadly 2020 encounter  shows lane king and tau also at the  scene as chauvin kneels on floyd's neck  lane and king had been on the force for  less than a week  at the heart of this case is whether or  not the defendants could and should have  tried to stop chauvin in minnesota the  only person that has to render any aid  would be the good samaritan laws but  they don't apply to police officers  in minnesota the troubled relationship  between police and the community goes  beyond the death of george floyd just  last month former brooklyn center police  officer kim potter was convicted of  manslaughter in the shooting death of  dante wright and now we have these three  former officers it's quite a unique  confluence of all of these issues  dealing with police officer and  community relations  derek shovit could make an appearance at  this trial it is possible that he is  called to testify by either the  prosecution or the defense but at this  point it's unclear if either side will  do that if convicted these three  officers could face up to life in prison  tony  a lot of healing still needs to happen  there in minnesota and the search for  justice is part of it mola thank you  very much
 

